# ENG-328: Proxmox's SDN code sets rp_filter=2 (loose) on each dynamically
# created EVPN fabric interface (vrfbr_*, vrfvx_*) at creation time,
# overriding net/ipv4/conf/default/rp_filter=0 set in 99-forwarding.conf -
# that default only applies to interfaces that don't get an explicit value
# set some other way. Confirmed live: even loose (2) silently drops
# externally-sourced packets arriving via the VXLAN fabric on these
# interfaces that need to route out to a VNet (asymmetric by nature of
# EVPN/ECMP) - packet arrives correctly addressed, but the destination's
# ARP/neighbor entry is never even probed, i.e. the routing decision
# itself never gets attempted. Matches a documented Proxmox forum report
# of the identical symptom (EVPN SDN not forwarding traffic to host with
# CT).
#
# Deliberately scoped to the fabric-facing interfaces only (vrfbr_*,
# vrfvx_*), NOT vnetNNN (the tenant-facing VNet interfaces) - rp_filter is
# an ingress check, and the packets in question arrive on the fabric
# interfaces, not the VNet ones. Confirmed live: reverting vnetNNN back to
# Proxmox's default (2) does not reintroduce the drop. Leaving Proxmox's
# own anti-spoofing default in place on the VM-facing interfaces rather
# than disabling rp_filter everywhere, since that protection is real and
# this fix doesn't need to remove it there.
#
# Since these interfaces are recreated by SDN reloads (not just at boot),
# a one-time sysctl.d file isn't enough - this has to re-fire on every
# interface creation. See docs/tickets/eng-322-vrf-evpnz1-ipv4-snat.md.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="net", KERNEL=="vrfbr_*", RUN+="/usr/sbin/sysctl -w net.ipv4.conf.%k.rp_filter=0"
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="net", KERNEL=="vrfvx_*", RUN+="/usr/sbin/sysctl -w net.ipv4.conf.%k.rp_filter=0"
